# Session Isolation Rule

Use this rule whenever multiple Cursor chats, agents, worktrees, or cloud agents
may touch this repo at the same time.

## Start-of-Task Boundary

Before substantial work, state the active boundary:

- Workflow or intent.
- Current branch / worktree when relevant.
- Files or directories expected to be touched.
- Whether this is read-only, draft-only, or write-capable work.

If the task may edit files and another session may be active, prefer a separate
git worktree or cloud agent branch. Do not create branches or worktrees without
the user's approval.

## Source of Truth

- Treat repo artifacts, live file contents, git status, diffs, and explicit user
  instructions as source of truth.
- Do not treat another session's chat transcript as fact unless the user
  explicitly asks to inspect it.
- If using a transcript for handoff, summarize it into an artifact under
  `ops/sessions/` before relying on it for future work.

## File Overlap Check

Before editing, check whether the intended files overlap with visible uncommitted
changes, session status files, or user-provided boundaries. If overlap exists,
work with the existing changes and call it out before editing.

## System-Affecting Changes

Flag these before editing because they affect future sessions:

- `.cursor/rules/**`
- `AGENTS.md`
- `docs/WORKFLOW_PATTERNS.md`
- `docs/CONTEXT_STRATEGY.md`
- `docs/HUMAN_GATES.md`
- shared templates under `content/templates/`, `research/templates/`, or
  `ops/templates/`

## Handoff

For concurrent work, keep a small status artifact in `ops/sessions/` with goal,
owner, branch / worktree, files touched, blockers, next step, and handoff notes.
Update it when the task boundary changes or before ending a session.
